# The unstable list of docs/provisional.md (section 1), as data: the features that Davis may still change and the 1.0.x compatibility
# promise does not cover (docs/releasing.md, Compatibility). The compiler warns when a program uses one (kind `unstable`, docs/errors.md,
# D121a); tests/run.sh checks that this file and section 1 of docs/provisional.md list the same features. This is the one place the list is
# kept: to add or remove a feature, change a row here and the table there, nothing else. A new row may be added only for a placeholder
# (docs/provisional.md says so).
#
# One feature for each row, four fields joined by `|`:
#   id      U1, U2, ...: the number in the first column of docs/provisional.md, which the warning quotes
#   what    the feature in words, as the warning names it
#   names   the std names that mean a use of it, `module.name` joined by commas; none for a feature that no program text can show
#           (the wording of messages, the host's input protocol)
#   change  what may change, as one phrase the warning gives
export def unstable_rows() -> list[str]:
    return [
        'U1|error message wording||the words of messages, help lines and warnings may be reworded (the error id and the class stay)',
        'U2|the host input protocol (TOMATO_INPUT_ASK, exit code 75)||the way a host asks a program for a line of input may change',
        'U3|the text progress_bar draws|itertools.progress_bar|the line the bar draws may change, for example to show the speed and the time left',
        'U4|random.choice, random.shuffle and random.sample|random.choice,random.shuffle,random.sample|they may become methods, such as rng.choice(items)',
    ]
